238: In the primitive case b=1, the exterior W and its boundary E have
239: 
240:     H1(W)=H2(W)=H3(W)=Z, H4(W)=0,
241:     H1(E)=H2(E)=H3(E)=Z^2, H4(E)=Z.
242: 
243: In the exported H2 basis z1,z2 the actual fibre is p z1 and
244: the exterior inclusion is (0,1). The second column is primitive:
245: its actual relative-Wang cycle is p(T O-O), corrected integrally
246: in the removed A_(p-1) root lattice. It has free cokernel value
247: plus or minus one. The original line M has values 7,15,10 in
248: the respective cokernels; it has not been substituted for that
249: primitive cycle.
250: 
251: In the good-root weighted cases b=p,
252: 
253:     H1(W)=Z, H2(W)=Z/p + Z, H3(W)=Z, H4(W)=0,
254:     H1(E)=H2(E)=Z/p + Z^2, H3(E)=Z^2, H4(E)=Z.
255: 
256: Use the exported H2 coordinates (eta,z1,z2), with eta of order
257: p and actual F=z1. The inclusions into (tau,z) of W are exactly
258: 
259:     OS47, III: [ [-1,-7,-1], [0,0,1] ],
260:     OS56, III: [ [-1,-15,-1], [0,0,1] ],
261:     OS56, IV:  [ [-2,-10,-2], [0,0,1] ].             (OA.2)
262: 
263: The torsion row is taken modulo p. In particular the torsion
264: boundary maps are units, and F generates exterior torsion. The
265: line M has nonzero removed-component degrees in these cases;
266: it is retained as a cohomology functional on V, not as a compact
267: cycle in its kernel lattice.
268: 
269: For both cases the exported H3 basis is precisely the oriented
270: source boundary L and the actual fibre-gamma trace F gamma.
271: Its exterior map is (0,1). These marked chain representatives
272: are stored in the JSON. This also fixes the D3 sign below.
273: 
274: ## OA.4. Cap specialization and all Mayer--Vietoris degrees
275: 
276: In the reduced case the cap source is a tree of p rational
277: components, cyclically permuted by the actual H. Its orbit cap
278: has H1=Zh, H2=Zc, H3=Z(sum C_i), H4=0. The actual generic
279: fibre specializes to sum C_i, hence its image in the coinvariants
280: is p c. As the boundary fibre is p z1 and the target is free,
281: z1 maps to c. Write the retained second cap column as kappa c.
282: The complete degree-two MV matrix, with source rows first, is
283: 
284:     D2 = [ [0,1], [-1,-kappa] ], det=1.              (OA.3)
285: 
286: No value or vanishing of the collar coefficient kappa is assumed.
287: 
288: In the good case the central elliptic monodromy is D^u, where
289: nu+mv=1. The cap has H1=Zh + Z/p, H2=ZE0, H3=Z(E0 h),
290: H4=0. Generic elliptic transport in the actual smooth root maps
291: F to E0 with degree one. The source lattice transport maps the
292: boundary torsion isomorphically to the cap torsion: for order
293: four u is odd and D^u-I differs from D-I by a unimodular
294: factor; for order three D+I=-D^2 supplies that factor. Thus
295: the torsion and source marking have been compared by actual
296: root transport. The H2 cap row is (0,1,kappa). Together with
297: (OA.2), the torsion row is an isomorphism and the remaining
298: free block is [[0,1],[-1,-kappa]], hence the full D2 is an
299: integral isomorphism for every retained kappa.
300: 
301: The H1 boundary torsion in the good case also maps isomorphically
302: to the cap's Z/p and to zero in W. After eliminating precisely
303: this actual isomorphism, the free degree-one matrix in the
304: marked basis (q,gamma_out) is
305: 
306:     D1 = [ [0,1], [n,-m] ].                         (OA.4)
307: 
308: In degree three, the cap source boundary maps to -n times its
309: primitive invariant fibre trace and F gamma maps to m times
310: that trace. This follows by its actual norm projection
311: u_cap=m u_ordinary-n arg(q)/(2pi), followed by the degree-one
312: specialization of the invariant sum C_i (reduced case) or E0
313: (good case). The cap source retracts to a two-dimensional
314: fibre, so there is no additional H3 source term. Therefore
315: 
316:     D3 = [ [0,1], [n,-m] ]                         (OA.5)
317: 
318: in the stored (L,F gamma) boundary basis. Finally D4 is
319: Z->0 and D0 is the incidence column (1,-1)^t. This lists
320: every MV degree, including the pre-elimination finite groups.
321: 
322: Van Kampen kills all elliptic generators in V. The cap's finite
323: elliptic group in the good case is killed by the same primitive
324: boundary transport. The remaining presentation has q=1 in W,
325: q=h^(-n), gamma=h^m, so pi1(Y)=Z/|n| (Z for n=0).
326: The integral MV sequence gives H0=H5=Z,
327: H1=H3=Z/|n| and H2=H4=0 for n nonzero. For n=0 (possible
328: only at the reduced order-one cap) it gives the corresponding
329: free kernel and cokernel groups directly from (OA.4)--(OA.5).
330: Thus the sphere members in these six one-cap sectors are exactly
331: n=+1 or -1. For those values, the simply connected integral
332: homology sphere Y is the standard S5. Its actual delta line
333: and the single selected I1 fixed sphere satisfy the Gysin and
334: Hopf-filling calculation of P3K.22, giving the standard S6
335: total space. For |n|>1 the same primitive Hopf meridian kills
336: only the circle kernel, leaving pi1(X)=Z/|n| and excluding a
337: sphere member.
338: 
339: All statements here retain the one-cap domain in OA.1. Multiple
340: additive caps and their signed Seifert determinant require their
341: joint boundary presentation. Return indices require the actual
342: parameter/page line comparison and are not inferred from these
343: topology matrices.
